    note: 'Ten currents through the Tibetan esoteric disciplines: the ritual grammar of the Vajrayāna, the two great traditions of direct approach, the anatomy they work upon, and the sciences of death, protection, calculation and revelation that grew around them. Technical terms are given in Tibetan script with Wylie transliteration, and Sanskrit equivalents where the Tibetan renders one; every Tibetan string here has been checked character by character against the Unicode Tibetan block. These are living traditions with living adherents, and much of what follows — empowerment, the completion stage, tögal, transference, the inner-heat practices — is transmitted only in person and only from a qualified teacher. What is set out here is description and history. It contains no instruction, and no operative detail is given for any practice.',
